      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "One important application of mixture models involves the use of marker data to map QTLs (Chapters 14–16). Here estimates of the category identity are influenced not only by an individual's trait value z but also by its marker genotype value m. For example, suppose a single diallelic QTL (with alleles Q, q) is linked to a marker, and an inbred-line cross is used in an attempt to map and characterize this QTL. In this case, the likelihood for an individual with marker genotype m and trait value z is",
