    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ Q_k $ denotes the $ k $th QTL genotype. The mixing proportions $ \\pi_k(m) $ are functions of the marker genotype, the QTL position (generally given by the marker-QTL recombination frequency distance $ c $), and the particular design used (see Example 6 below).",
      "source_page": 878,
      "printed_page": 858,
      "source_block_ids": [
